`cart.total()` was returning `"subtotal"` as the raw pre-discount amount while computing `tax` and `total` on the post-discount amount — so `subtotal + tax != total`, and any consumer that re-applied tax to `"subtotal"` would overcharge. Fixed by making `"subtotal"` the post-discount pre-tax base (so `subtotal + tax == total` always holds) and adding `"original_subtotal"` for the raw display amount. Added `tests/test_issue_2.py`; full suite green (42 passed).
